{{Politics of Balisca}}

The [[Balisca|Baliscan Confederation]] consists of seven historic [[W:Ethnolinguistics|ethnolinguistic]] '''communities''' ({{Lang-bl|comunidad}}) within it's borders. They first emerged during the [[colonization of Abyala]] in the 16th century, and were consolidated in the mid-1700s, when the original three [[W:Thalassocracy|thalassocratic]] communities ([[United Provinces of Bayara|Bayara]], [[Hesperia#Volisanya Boba|Hesperia]], and [[Commonwealth of Cerdanya|Cerdanya]]) voluntarily {{W|confederation|confederated}} with mutual recognition of the right to {{W|self-determination}}. Powers varied between these communities varied and largely depended on their economic power and {{W|geography|geographic}} location. Through the adoption of confederal compacts by these interdependent communities they adopted common defense and foreign policies, gradually consolidating politically in the early [[Volisanya Boba]] period. These highly decentralized "states" were linked only through their ethnolinguistic closeness, rather than mutual political allegiance.  

As a result of decades of sustained internal migration, [[Immigration to Balisca|immigration from overseas]], and the [[Cosmocazo|emergence]] of a [[Basic Laws of Balisca|Baliscan identity]], these nationalist divisions gradually [[W:post-nationalism|lost importance]] as Balisca adopted a [[Cosmocazo|cosmopolitan]] identity. The political power of these states were eventually [[1919 Confederal Convention|abolished]] in favor of [[W:Decentralization|decentralization]] after the [[Baliscan Revolution]].

[[Confederal Question|Prior to the 1830s]], the confederation did not have a powerful central government. Issues thought to affect the whole Confederation were the subject of periodic meetings in various locations. The Articles of Confederation (1810) provided few details concerning institutions, and this was not addressed until the [[1826 Confederal Convention]] in Alessandria. It was largely ineffective, as all [[Bayara|Bayaran]] provinces except [[Macaio|Carpinchera]] boycotted the congress. The [[Xunta Nacionalista|Bayaran secession]] and [[Baliscan Civil War|mobilization]] against the Congress led to an early termination without an definitive agreement. Around the same time, Castejón was considered to be the {{W|frontier}} of the fledgling confederation, a settlement in the "middle ground" in between cultures, peoples, and beyond state control. Bayaran armies conducted a campaign to capture the [[Alpujarra]] in 1827, which culminated in the [[Siege of Castejón]] and saw the intervention of the [[Maroon Confederacy]].

